<div class="path-head"><p class="featured-region">Reading path · 7 stops</p><h1 class="path-title">The World Wars</h1><p class="path-tagline">Three decades that ended the age of empires.</p><p class="path-intro">Between 1914 and 1945 the states of Europe fought two wars that consumed the world and, in the end, their own empires. This path follows the arc from Sarajevo to Hiroshima: the war that broke four empires, the peace that failed, and the war that finished what the first began.</p><p class="path-types">Suits <a href="/start">the Strategist</a> · <a href="/start">the Timekeeper</a></p></div>
<ol class="path-steps"><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-world-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">1 · Encyclopedia · Event</span><span class="path-step-name">First World War</span><span class="path-step-why">Four years that killed four empires: Hohenzollern, Habsburg, Romanov and Ottoman.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">2 · Encyclopedia · Event</span><span class="path-step-name">Treaty of Versailles</span><span class="path-step-why">The peace that ended the war and seeded the next.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/german-empire"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/proclamation-of-the-german-empire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">3 · Profile · 1871 CE – 1918 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">German Empire</span><span class="path-step-why">The rising power whose fears and ambitions drove the July crisis of 1914.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/empire-of-japan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-meiji.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">4 · Profile · 1868 CE – 1945 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Empire of Japan</span><span class="path-step-why">The one non-European empire of the age, from Meiji ascent to 1945.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-world-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">5 · Encyclopedia · Event</span><span class="path-step-name">Second World War</span><span class="path-step-why">The deadliest war in history, and the end of Europe's centuries at the centre of the world.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/atomic-bombings-of-hiroshima-and-nagasaki"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/atomic-bombings-of-hiroshima-and-nagasaki.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">6 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1945</span><span class="path-step-name">Atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki</span><span class="path-step-why">The weeks that ended the war and opened an age in which great-power war risks everything.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/british-empire"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/slavery-abolition-act-1833.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">7 · Profile · 1583 CE – 1997 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">British Empire</span><span class="path-step-why">Victorious and exhausted: how winning two world wars still cost an empire.</span></span></a></li></ol>
